"""In-place ``_foreach_sin_`` for Ascend 910B (Triton).

Semantics reproduced from ATen ``aten::_foreach_sin_(Tensor(a!)[] self) -> ()``:

* every tensor in the list is mutated in place (``x[i] <- sin(x[i])``),
* storage pointer, shape, strides and dtype are unchanged,
* the call returns ``None``,
* non floating dtypes are rejected with the ATen cast error,
* an empty list is rejected,
* non contiguous but dense views (transposes) are addressed in flat memory
  order, gappy views go through a stride aware kernel, so no data is copied.

Architecture:

* ``sin`` is evaluated with an explicit range reduction (three part Cody-Waite
  split of pi) plus one odd degree-13 polynomial instead of ``tl.sin``, whose
  libdevice style expansion costs ~39 wide fp32 vector ops per element.
* all flat tensors sharing a dtype are fused into a single launch
  (``_sin_multi_kernel``, one grid axis selects the tensor, per-tensor base
  pointer and element count arrive as scalar kernel arguments), so the host
  pays one launch per 16-tensor batch instead of one per tensor.  The grid is
  derived from the work, never from the device core count.
"""

import torch
import triton
import triton.language as tl

_INT32_MAX = 2**31 - 1
_MAX_NT = 16


